WEBVTT

00:00:06.740 --> 00:00:08.400
Excuse me. Can you help me?

00:00:08.580 --> 00:00:09.660
Sure, what do you want?

00:00:10.200 --> 00:00:12.420
Where is 83 Wooster Street?

00:00:12.940 --> 00:00:15.780
That's easy. Walk to the corner.

00:00:16.080 --> 00:00:17.680
Then make a left turn.

00:00:18.060 --> 00:00:20.800
Then walk two blocks to the traffic light.

00:00:21.160 --> 00:00:22.500
Make another left to Wooster.

00:00:22.580 --> 00:00:23.420
Thank you.

00:00:24.100 --> 00:00:26.300
To the corner and then a left?

00:00:26.460 --> 00:00:27.540
Yeah. A left.

00:00:27.820 --> 00:00:29.480
Hot dog? Only seventy-five cents.

00:00:29.700 --> 00:00:31.720
No. Thank you. I have a dinner date.

00:00:47.280 --> 00:00:55.020
555-9470...and it's busy....

00:01:04.740 --> 00:01:12.640
555-9470...and it's still busy.

00:01:20.380 --> 00:01:21.780
Excuse me, ma'am.

00:01:22.050 --> 00:01:24.570
I'm looking for 83 Wooster Street.

00:01:25.010 --> 00:01:27.960
Yes. Wooster Street is two blocks,

00:01:28.360 --> 00:01:34.860
and 83 is to the right, about two houses.

00:01:35.220 --> 00:01:37.040
Thank you, thank you!

00:01:37.100 --> 00:01:37.960
You're welcome.

00:01:47.540 --> 00:01:48.720
Who is it?

00:01:48.960 --> 00:01:50.680
Harry Bennett. Is this Susan?

00:01:50.840 --> 00:01:52.220
Yes, it is. Come up.

00:01:52.320 --> 00:01:53.640
I'm on the top floor.

00:01:54.960 --> 00:01:58.030
Hello, Harry. It's nice to meet you.

00:01:58.040 --> 00:01:59.160
Nice to meet you, Susan.

00:02:00.180 --> 00:02:01.220
Sorry I'm late.

00:02:01.980 --> 00:02:06.160
The traffic. The parking. I was lost.

00:02:07.660 --> 00:02:09.900
What pretty flowers! Thank you.

00:02:10.080 --> 00:02:11.400
Oh, please come in.

00:02:12.460 --> 00:02:14.640
Don't worry about being late. It's fine.

00:02:16.340 --> 00:02:19.200
Excuse the mess. I just moved here.

00:02:19.720 --> 00:02:22.000
Oh, I'd like you to meet my sister-in-law Marilyn.

00:02:22.560 --> 00:02:24.740
Marilyn Stewart, this is Harry Bennett.

00:02:25.070 --> 00:02:25.900
Pleased to meet you.

00:02:25.900 --> 00:02:26.940
Nice to meet you, Harry.

00:02:27.460 --> 00:02:29.180
Are we too late for our dinner reservation?

00:02:29.720 --> 00:02:31.840
No, the restaurant will hold our table.

00:02:32.000 --> 00:02:33.160
I know the owner very well.

00:02:33.160 --> 00:02:33.960
I eat there a lot.

00:02:34.140 --> 00:02:35.620
Do you know the phone number of the restaurant?

00:02:36.240 --> 00:02:37.660
I'd like to call home

00:02:37.660 --> 00:02:39.020
and leave the number with the baby-sitter.

00:02:49.710 --> 00:02:50.560
May I use the phone?

00:03:06.650 --> 00:03:07.870
Hi, Michelle. It's Daddy.

00:03:07.980 --> 00:03:08.800
Can I speak to Betty?

00:03:10.160 --> 00:03:12.720
I want to leave the phone number of the restaurant...

00:03:13.990 --> 00:03:18.230
Hi, Betty. I'll be at five five five...seventeen twenty.

00:03:24.090 --> 00:03:26.170
Well, that's done. Shall we go?

00:03:26.600 --> 00:03:28.900
I'm ready. See you later, Marilyn.

00:03:29.040 --> 00:03:29.880
Have a nice evening.

00:03:30.680 --> 00:03:32.260
Bye, Marilyn. Hope to see you again.

00:03:32.520 --> 00:03:34.340
Me, too. Have fun!

00:03:34.880 --> 00:03:35.260
Thanks.

00:03:38.820 --> 00:03:39.740
After you.
